    "title": "Event-Driven Microservices",
    "systemTag": "COMMERCE PLATFORM // EVENT BACKBONE",
    "statusLabel": "REFERENCE ARCHITECTURE",
    "overviewSummary": "An order platform where services talk through events instead of calling each other. The Order Service writes the order and an outbox row in one transaction, then publishes OrderPlaced to a Kafka topic. Payment, fulfilment, notifications and a CQRS read model each consume it at their own pace. A failed payment publishes PaymentFailed and the Order Service compensates by cancelling the order (a choreographed saga). Shipping work goes through a FIFO queue with a dead-letter queue.",
